message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "The footprint of climate oscillations in global inland waters: analysis code and derived data"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis quantifying how the leading modes of interannual climate variability
  (ENSO, IOD and NAO) explain year-to-year temperature variability in global rivers and lakes
  (surface and bottom), 1950-2021. The oscillation footprint F is the fraction of detrended
  interannual water-temperature variance jointly explained by the three modes; field-significant
  cells are termed teleconnected. Includes code, derived GeoTIFF/JSON products and interactive tools.
